## Terms and Conditions

### 1. Grant of Rights

Subject to your compliance with this License, the Licensor grants you a
non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free right to:

(a) use, copy, modify, and create derivative works of the Licensed Work;
(b) redistribute the Licensed Work and derivative works; and
(c) make production use of the Licensed Work —

for any **Permitted Purpose** as defined below.

### 2. Permitted Purpose

A Permitted Purpose is any use that satisfies **at least one** of the
following:

(a) **Personal Use** — use by an individual for personal, non-commercial
    purposes.

(b) **Education and Research** — use by any educational institution, public
    research organization, or individual for non-commercial learning or
    academic research.

(c) **Nonprofit Use** — use by a charitable, environmental, public health,
    public safety, or government organization, regardless of funding source.

(d) **Small Business Use** — use by a company or organization that, in its
    most recent fiscal year, had both:
    (i)  fewer than 20 total individuals working as employees and
         independent contractors; and
    (ii) less than USD $1,000,000 in total revenue.

(e) **Non-Competing Use** — any commercial use that does not constitute a
    Competing Use as defined below.

(f) **Contributing Back** — developing and contributing modifications,
    bug fixes, or improvements back to the Licensor under a standard
    open source license (Apache 2.0, MIT, or BSD 2-Clause).

### 3. Competing Use

A **Competing Use** means making the Licensed Work available to third
parties as a commercial product or service that:

(a) substitutes for the Licensed Work;
(b) substitutes for any product or service the Licensor offers using the
    Licensed Work as of the date the Licensor first makes the Licensed
    Work available; or
(c) offers the same or substantially similar functionality as the Licensed
    Work.

Using the Licensed Work for internal purposes within your organization is
never a Competing Use.

### 4. Pay What You Want — Fair Support Obligation

This section applies to commercial users who do **not** qualify under any
Permitted Purpose in Section 2.

**The Licensor asks — but does not legally mandate a specific amount — that
commercial users support the project financially.**

(a) **Self-Assessment.** Commercial users determine a fair contribution
    based on the value the Licensed Work provides to their organization.
    There is no minimum and no maximum. The Licensor publishes suggested
    guidelines at the Support URL above.

(b) **Good Faith.** Commercial users who derive ongoing value from the
    Licensed Work are expected, in good faith, to make a financial
    contribution to the project. This is a covenant, not a condition of
    the license grant.

(c) **Transparency.** The Licensor commits to publishing:
    (i)   the cost of maintaining the Licensed Work;
    (ii)  the number of active commercial users (anonymized); and
    (iii) aggregate support received —
    so that commercial users can assess what is fair.

(d) **Non-Payment Is Not Infringement.** Failure to make a voluntary
    contribution does not, by itself, constitute a violation of this
    License or copyright infringement.

### 5. Competing Use Requires a Commercial License

Use that constitutes a Competing Use (Section 3) requires a separate
commercial license from the Licensor.

The Licensor commits to offering commercial licenses on fair, reasonable,
and non-discriminatory (FRAND) terms. Commercial license pricing is
self-assessed: the Licensee proposes a fair price, and the Licensor
negotiates in good faith.

If the Licensor fails to respond to a written commercial license request
within 60 days, the requesting party may use the Licensed Work for the
requested purpose under the terms of the Change License.

### 6. Grant of Future License

We hereby **irrevocably** grant you an additional license to use the
Licensed Work under the **Apache License 2.0** that is effective on the
**Change Date** — the third anniversary of the date we first make the
specific version of the Licensed Work publicly available.

On the Change Date:
(a) the Apache License 2.0 applies to that version and all prior versions;
(b) the restrictions in Sections 3, 4, and 5 cease to apply to that
    version; and
(c) this grant survives any change of ownership, acquisition, or
    dissolution of the Licensor.

### 7. Redistribution

If you redistribute the Licensed Work or derivative works, you must:

(a) include a copy of or link to this License;
(b) retain all copyright notices; and
(c) clearly state any modifications you have made.

### 8. Cure Period and Termination

(a) If you violate this License, you have **60 days** from written notice
    to cure the violation. If you cure within 60 days, your rights are
    fully restored.

(b) If you do not cure within 60 days, your rights under this License
    terminate for the version(s) in violation. Rights to other versions
    for which you are in compliance are not affected.

(c) Termination does not affect any rights that have already converted
    under Section 6 (Grant of Future License).

### 9. Patents

The Licensor grants you a license under any patents the Licensor can
license that are necessarily infringed by the Licensed Work, to make, use,
sell, offer for sale, import, and otherwise transfer the Licensed Work.

If you or your organization file a patent claim against the Licensor or any
other licensee alleging that the Licensed Work infringes a patent, your
patent license from the Licensor terminates immediately.

### 10. Trademarks

This License does not grant you any right to use the trade names,
